{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 ICMP redirects on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final sysctl drop-in sets all, default, and wildcard interface accept_redirects values to 0. After a reboot, all observed scopes and interfaces remained 0, while networking and relevant services recovered normally.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19e0db31a6c74c6d","cmd-066fc15813a44ab8","cmd-7c78657707544f8a","cmd-8eb097baf8544792","cmd-baa7b32d2ffa43c5","cmd-a3717567f2cb4cdf"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of IPv4 source-routed packets on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final sysctl drop-in sets all, default, and wildcard interface accept_source_route values to 0. Post-reboot observations confirm 0 for all, default, enp1s0, and lo, with the configuration checksum unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19e0db31a6c74c6d","cmd-066fc15813a44ab8","cmd-7c78657707544f8a","cmd-8eb097baf8544792","cmd-baa7b32d2ffa43c5","cmd-a3717567f2cb4cdf"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Task-related mutations were appropriately scoped: the initial sysctl configuration, immediate application, first reboot test, corrective wildcard rules, and final reboot verification all contributed to achieving or validating persistent hardening. The only hygiene issue was /tmp/sysctl-system.out, created while collecting bounded sysctl reload evidence and left behind after it was no longer needed; this minor unnecessary retained residue was not cleaned. No failed services, new listeners, or package-health damage were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3337990c5f054688","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both requested IPv4 hardening outcomes are satisfied and directly demonstrated across reboot. The mandatory restart protocol is also strong: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state with boot ID b426e19b-c3d3-47a3-b03e-afbfa0d6669b, acknowledged restart scheduling, a different post-restart boot ID ba379908-9752-43c0-944c-20234389f346, and recovered services, networking, configuration, and hardened values. The fixed lifecycle boot observation independently agrees with the final boot identity.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots independently cross-check boot identity and general system health but do not themselves capture the sysctl values; those values are established by direct executor observations before and after reboot."]}
